# 7/6/2025
I'd like to talk about a job that I wouldn't enjoy doing, which is being a coach driver.

I first thought about this job when I was in high school. At that time, I took a sleeper bus with some of my close friends to visit Da Lat, which is quite far from where I live. The journey took around seven hours, so we had to leave late at night, at about 11 p.m.

During the trip, I happened to sit near the driver and had a conversation with him. He told me that although he had been doing the job for many years, he didn't actually enjoy it. However, he continued working because he needed to financially support his family. Hearing that left a strong impression on me.

One reason I wouldn't want to do this job is that it's both stressful and risky. Coach drivers are responsible for the safety of dozens of passengers, so they need to stay focused for long periods of time. Many of them work overnight and may not get enough sleep, which can have negative effects on their health in the long run.

Another drawback is the demanding work schedule. Coach drivers often have to work at night, on weekends, or during public holidays. As a result, they may miss important family events and have less time to spend with their loved ones.

Overall, while I respect people who do this job, I don't think it would suit me because of the high level of responsibility, irregular working hours, and potential health risks.

